---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';

const title = 'Write Your Novel Fast';
const description = 'Articles &amp; Ideas to help you write your novel.';
const permalink = Astro.site.href;
---
<BaseLayout title={title} description={description} permalink={permalink}>
  <div class="home-container">
     <div class="home-copy">
        <h1>Test Your Novel Ideas </h1>
        <p>First Draft: 2026-07-25 -- this will be updated often</p>
        <h2>The Fastest Way To Get Your Novel Written</h2>
        <p>Fail Fast - To get better at anything you must do a lot of it.  However, as humans
        we hate to "waste time".  Many writers think, "Why would I write a novel unless I know it
        will be good and successful?"</p>
        <p>That is how I always failed: I got stuck in my mind, thinking about writing and knowing it wouldn't be perfect and figuring it wouldn't be successful, so I never took action and actually wrote the entire novel.</p>
        <blockquote>
        "No one ever became perfect through inaction." ~anonymous
        </blockquote>
        <p>It's really quite limiting because it instantly freezes
        you up from writing anything - even one sentence.  It's because you're stuck on the thought 
        that "if it doesn't succeed, then it's a waste of time".</p>
        <p>Imagine if you looked at every task like that.  Suppose you thought that when:
        <ul>
           <li>Learning to ride a bike</li>
           <li>Learning to catch a ball</li>
           <li>Learning to drive a car</li>
           <li>Learning to read</li>
        </ul>
        </p>
        <p>This is really the <strong>terrible philosophy</strong> of "What would you do if you knew you couldn't fail?"</p>
        <p>That philosophy turned upside down is "Why do anything unless you know you'll succeed?"</p>
        <p>Well, I guess you shouldn't ever try anything you're unsure of, which means you're probably going to sit on your couch doomscrolling.</p>
        <p> <a href="" target="_blank"></a>.
        </p>
        <h2>Learn the Creative Way To Test If Your Novel Idea Is A Good One</h2>

        <p></p>

        <p></p>

        <p></p>
        <h2>Read the Blog, Read The Book</h2>
   <p></p>
   <p> <a href="about">About page.</a></p>
   <h2></h2>
   <p></p>
   <p></p>

    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .home-container {
    align-items: center;
    display: flex;
    flex: 1;
    justify-content: center;
    margin: 2em 0;
    min-height: 400px;
  }

  .home-copy {
    flex: 1;
    padding: 0 1em;
  }

  .home-copy h1 {
    font-weight: 700;
    margin-bottom: 0.5em;
    line-height: 1.3;
  }

  .home-copy p {
    font-size: 1.4em;
  }

  .hero-image-container {
    margin: 0 1em;
    text-align: center;
  }

  .hero-image-container picture {
    display: block;
    min-height: 250px;
  }

  .caption {
    font-size: .8em;
    font-style: italic;
    text-align: left;
  }

  .hero-image {
    width: 100%;
    max-width: 550px;
    margin-bottom: 1em;
  }

  @media (max-width: 1200px) {
    p {
      font-size: 1.2em;
    }

    .hero-image {
      max-width: 400px;
    }
  }

  @media (max-width: 800px) {
    .home-container {
      flex-direction: column;
    }

    .home-copy {
      flex: 0;
      padding-bottom: 2em;
      text-align: center;
    }
  }
</style>
